  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing due diligence monitoring and reporting in Morocco#s automotive industry</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. As part of the new strategic priorities, one of the focus areas is on sustainable supply chains. Accordingly, the new priority was also reflected in the Organization#s new organogram with the establishment of IET/PST/SSB. This unit has launched its activities with internal stocktaking and reaching out to possible partner entities involved in sustainable supply chains, such as the International Trade Centre (ITC), OECD, Amfori, ILO and others. 2. IET/PST/SSB has also concuptialized and identified the UNIDO competences in comparison with other agencies, such as the strong field presence, ability to deliver services in environmental standards, skills development, responsible investment, certification services and SME support based on voluntary sustainability standards. 3. During the UNIDO-Germany High-Level Dialogue in December 2022, USD 500,000 was earmarked to UNIDO to collaborate under the Initiative for Global Solidarity (IGS) implemented by GIZ. IGS focuses on developing sustainable supply chains in four pilot countries (Bangladesh, Cambodia, Serbia and Vietnam). 4. This project will be the first outcome of the PA 220220 formulation. GIZ indicated during the preliminary discussion that this project as part of the Initiative for Global Solidarity (IGS) should focus on SME upgrade with special attention on w</narrative>
  </description>
